    "answer": {
        "text": "§\nDescribe how dietary Vitamin D is converted into the active form\n\n(1) 25-hydroxylated in the liver\n(2) 1-hydroxylated in the kidney\n\n(∴ Calcitriol would be indicated over Vit. D2/D3 in the setting of renal/liver disease)\n\n[Image: f78a156bb349082af59265500f2ae031868e7f4a3ec7baa11abc2e93af83b8e2]\n\n[Image: 1441600308dce9c28dbbe2a927c865519bd877425637357ca4674006ffbb5a35]\n\n3.3 - Teriparatide, vitamin D, cinacalcet, sevelame\n\n[Image: 4298e78b27c77e9be26a3315ef94e1449bf4f3333203dd64aef50652cce9b080]\n\n[Image: 0d8bcf50b941d06eb3acedd71ef95ad2c633d03d05e1929b321aca54170c2656]\n\n[Image: bb7a366363f2144f1f342d3ac611c281babe1fc0ee8b93a96e580f11239e27e0]\n\n[Image: 34b2bdc6643b813866ff83567203f474ad3825f2c882e94a70b0cd9de3de00b8]\n\n[Image: 828e4d13e74c599b9c1305dc0515e1887e6211fb43b59d6204b47d3295896812]\n\n[Image: 6f4f86b7c169893f2937f2037815d3a00709b32594507ec3dd69174ba87e529f]\n\n[Image: a0bfadc2893d1cd305662d9c6ec962516c32c4ad80863ee55ec1d667ad61a421]",
